messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: apps/lib/log.c
Line: 49
Function: log_with_prefix
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: BIO_snprintf(prefix, sizeof(prefix), "%s: ", prog) uses the %s format specifier on 'prog' without checking for NULL. A concrete path exists: log_set_verbosity(NULL, invalid_level) calls trace_log_message(-1, prog, LOG_ERR, ...), which (with default verbosity >= LOG_ERR) calls log_with_prefix and dereferences the NULL 'prog', causing a crash.

Source context:
